<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;DOUGLAS COUNTY COURTHOUSE (NEBRASKA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Douglas County Courthouse (Nebraska) is located at 1701 Farnam Street in Omaha, Nebraska, United States. It was built in 1912 and added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1979."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE SECOND COURTHOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The second courthouse was used until the current one was finished in 1912 and then was torn down with some materials being reused in various projects around Omaha."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OMAHA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Omaha is the location where some materials from the second courthouse were reused in various projects."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURRENT COURTHOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The current courthouse was finished in 1912 and replaced the second courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLAY COUNTY COURTHOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clay County Courthouse is a neoclassical structure built in 1912, replacing the previous courthouse without substantial modification."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINTON COUNTY COURTHOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinton County Courthouse is a replacement for a 150-year-old previous courthouse, built in 1999."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLES COUNTY COURTHOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coles County Courthouse is located in Charleston and is mentioned alongside other courthouses, suggesting it is also a location of interest."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHARLESTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Charleston is the location of Coles County Courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOUISVILLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Louisville is mentioned as a location, though no specific courthouse is associated with it in this text."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clay is the location of Clay County Courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinton is the location of Clinton County Courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coles is the location of Coles County Courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1912&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1912 marks the year the current courthouse was finished and the second courthouse was torn down."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1999&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1999 marks the year the Clinton County Courthouse was built, replacing a 150-year-old previous courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;150 YEARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"150 years is the approximate age of the previous courthouse that was replaced by the Clinton County Courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEOCLASSICAL STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ARCHITECTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neoclassical structure describes the style of the Clay County Courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REMODELLING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ACTIVITY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Remodelling refers to the process of building the Clay County Courthouse under the guise of remodelling the previous courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REUSED MATERIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"RESOURCE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reused materials refer to the materials from the second courthouse that were reused in various projects around Omaha."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PREVIOUS COURTHOUSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Previous courthouse refers to the courthouse that existed before the current one and the second courthouse."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0407-dc7e1db5c944</data>
    </node>
